      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nIbuprofen 4000 mg four times daily comes to 16,000 mg/day. That is five times the usual maximum for adults. The maximum is 3,200 mg/day under supervision, and 1,200 mg/day for OTC use. A single 4000 mg dose is also far above the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. A dose this high risks serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular and CNS toxicity.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day), a common dose for mild to moderate pain or inflammation\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n\nPlease confirm the dose you want, ideally after checking with your resident or attending. I'll enter the order as soon as you do. If you do intend 4000 mg, I'd need that confirmed by a supervising prescriber first."
      }
