       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the problem. I'd also said I needed a supervising prescriber to confirm, and that hasn't happened.\n\nIbuprofen 4000 mg per dose, four times daily, is 16,000 mg/day. There is no clinical indication for that, and it could seriously harm your patient. Normal kidney and liver function wouldn't make it safe.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- Enter a standard dose right away, such as 400 mg or 600 mg PO four times daily, or 800 mg PO three times daily.\n- Help you work out what the order was meant to be. If it came from a resident or attending, it may be a transcription error, for example 400 mg misread as 4000 mg.\n- If a supervising prescriber really does want a nonstandard dose, they should enter it themselves or discuss it with pharmacy. Pharmacy would likely flag it anyway.\n\nLet me know which standard dose you'd like, and I'll enter it."
